# R0 entry gate — frozen closure evidence
#
# Reference: docs/development/learning-roadmap-r1-r8-w5-w6.md line 35 ("R0 entry
# gate") and the quantitative promotion-gate table at line 294.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
# -----------------
# The roadmap says no behaviour-changing slice (R1-R8, W5-W6) may be PROMOTED
# until findings 9, 11, 17, and 40-43 from reports/core-audit-2026-07-11.md have
# verified closure evidence, and that closure must be recorded as immutable
# evidence references rather than inferred from the roadmap prose.
#
# This is that record, in a form a script can re-verify. It is consumed by
# scripts/check-r0-entry-gate.sh, which runs in CI (job `r0-entry-gate` in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml) and as step 8 of scripts/ci-gate.sh. If a
# prerequisite regresses -- an anchor deleted, a defect signature reintroduced,
# a behavioural test removed, a closure commit no longer in history -- the gate
# goes red and R0 reverts to OPEN.
#
# This file is APPEND-CORRECT, not append-only: an entry may be edited only to
# record a REGRESSION (verdict -> open) or to add evidence. Rewriting a closed
# entry's commit or verdict to make a red gate green is the exact fraud this
# file exists to make visible in review.
#
# FORMAT
# ------
#   [finding:<id>]        starts a block
#   key = value           one directive per line; '#' starts a comment line
#
# Directives:
#   title            one-line restatement of the audit finding
#   verdict          closed | open      (gate fails unless every block is closed)
#   verification     mechanical | manual
#   attested_by      REQUIRED when verification = manual; a named human
#   commit           <40-hex sha>  <subject>   pushed commit that closed it
#   anchor           <path> :: <ERE>   must be PRESENT in path
#   absent           <path> :: <ERE>   must be ABSENT from path (defect signature)
#   order            <path> :: <ERE-first> :: <ERE-second>
#                    first match of ERE-first must precede first match of
#                    ERE-second in path
#   wired            <path> :: <ERE>   live call site; same check as anchor,
#                    reported separately because this repo has repeatedly
#                    shipped correct code nothing calls (#76, #129, #161)
#   test             <path> :: <fn>    behavioural test that must still exist
#   source_of_truth  <path> :: <fn>    test that reads the persisted/streamed
#                    artefact back rather than trusting the writer's return
#   deviation        recorded, not checked: how the shipped fix differs from
#                    the fix the audit proposed
#   note             recorded, not checked
#
# Every required finding must carry at least one commit, anchor, wired, test and
# source_of_truth directive; the checker enforces that, so an entry cannot be
# thinned out to a title and a verdict.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
