deviation = MATERIAL, and the one the issue asked to be called out. The audit
deviation = proposed similarity-searching existing CorrectionDerived rules and
deviation = reinforcing the closest, with rule text synthesised per correction
deviation = via template or LLM. What shipped is stronger and simpler: the rule
deviation = identity is a compile-time constant per CorrectionType, so there is
deviation = no similarity threshold to tune and no synthesis step to go wrong,
deviation = and raw user text can never reach a rule body at all. The cost is
deviation = coarser granularity: five generic rules instead of a growing set of
deviation = correction-specific ones. R2/R3 lesson provenance must therefore
deviation = come from the correction records, not from rule text.

