# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same clause of the same gate, one slice later. Slice 3 (R2) adds a causal
# attribution engine, and the gate's condition applies to it unchanged: it may
# measure, it may not mutate rules. Slice 3 also does the opposite of adding a
# mutation -- it REMOVES one, by gating the correction-driven rule boost on an
# attribution that succeeded. A restriction does not need the gate's permission,
# but it does need a tripwire, because silently restoring the old ordering would
# put every unexplained correction back into the rule scores.
